  "text" : "You only need four ideas from linear algebra to understand what AI models are doing.\nA vector is a MOV. Its numbers are the recipe. Amounts along directions that we all agreed on.\nA matrix says where those directions land. Multiplying rebuilds that recipe in the new directions.\nIn PyTorch, x at w is just that. Each number in x weights a row of w and adds them up.\nA dot product measures alignment. Attention scores are dot products between queries and keys of your tokens.\nIn a neural network, those matrices are learned, layer by layer.\nTraining finds which directions to amplify, which to ignore, and which ones to mix.\nThe model doesn't understand in a human way, it learns moves that make the task easier.\nVectors hold information, matrices reshape it into the forms the model can use."
